Figure 1. Positions of the Earth (SDO and SOHO) and STEREO in the ecliptic plane on 2014 June 14 and their observations.
(Top Left) EUVI-B 195 Å image, showing the source location of solar eruption. (Bottom Left) AIA 193 Å image, confirming a
limb event from the Earth perspective. (Top right) GOES soft X-ray 1-8 Å flux, displaying an M1.4 class flare. (Bottom right)
LASCO C2 image, presenting a CME without the typical three-part structure.



